{
    "title": "AWS AppSync Merged API over two source APIs backed by Amazon DynamoDB",
    "description": "An AWS AppSync Merged API combines two source GraphQL APIs, each backed by its own Amazon DynamoDB table and protected by AWS IAM, into one endpoint using AUTO_MERGE.",
    "language": "TypeScript",
    "level": "300",
    "framework": "AWS CDK",
    "patternGroup": "appsync-merged-api",
    "introBox": {
        "headline": "How it works",
        "text": [
            "Two AWS AppSync source GraphQL APIs, an Orders API and a Customers API, each read from their own Amazon DynamoDB table through an APPSYNC_JS resolver. An AWS AppSync Merged API associates both with AUTO_MERGE and exposes one AWS_IAM endpoint.",
            "The Customers schema adds an Order.customer field to the Order type owned by the Orders API, so one GraphQL document returns an order and its customer from two tables.",
            "The merge execution role is scoped to the two source API ARNs (appsync:SourceGraphQL) and the two association ARNs (appsync:StartSchemaMerge). The request path has no AWS Lambda function."
        ]
    },
    "gitHub": {
